items.test:
test/unit/renderer-command.test.ts. Three source-regex checks are replaced by value tests that drive the code with fakes:
- applyTextScale's calls and their order: no-op when unchanged, every terminal and then one report with the new scale, NaN counts as the default;
- a new terminal's fontSize at each scale (13/15/17), checked with a fake xterm;
- cellSize's result from a fake measuring host against the measured cells, plus the font size and family it measures at;
- with a fake xterm that redraws its grid as xterm does (931x312 -> 712x234), setTextScale(1) from Larger moves the hidden input onto cell (90,12) inside the new grid, and the same size again redraws nothing.

One source pin stays: the observer's attributeFilter and its applyTextScale call. The new tests failed before (applyTextScale missing; the stand-in was ignored). Each one also fails when its wiring is broken on purpose: grid read after the font changes, no scale passed to new terminals, the cell measured at 13 px, report before the terminals, no early return, the input not moved. Each break fails exactly one test.

test/unit/page-prefs.test.ts, 'grows the height of every control with words with them…'. The guard was widened from fixedButtonHeights to fixedControlHeights. It covers:
- button, select, textarea and text inputs by element;
- each page's own controls, by the ids in its index.html;
- a height or min-height in px, inside media queries too.

Check boxes, radios, sliders and pseudo-elements are left out. The test also pins the default lengths. With the CSS stashed it failed: home: ['.models select', '.choice select', '#text-size', '.add-row input']. It passes now.

